# Testing
- **Framework**: use the one already in the project (Vitest/Jest, xUnit/NUnit/MSTest, pytest).
  Do not add a second one.
- **Pyramid**: many fast unit tests, fewer integration tests, few end-to-end tests. Test at the
  lowest level that proves the behaviour.
- **Bug fixes**: start with a failing test that reproduces the bug.
- **Names**: describe the behaviour (`Returns404WhenApplicationMissing`).
- **Structure**: arrange, act, assert, with one behaviour per test. No loops or ifs in tests.
- **Isolation**: deterministic and order-independent. No real network or clock; use doubles at
  the boundaries.
- **Data access**: when query semantics matter, test against SQLite in-memory or a test
  container. EF's InMemory provider hides SQL behaviour.
- **Coverage**: every acceptance criterion maps to at least one test.
